          <p>A meteoroid is a small rocky or metallic body in space. When it enters Earth's atmosphere and creates a streak of light, it becomes a meteor (or shooting star). If it survives the journey and lands on Earth, it is called a meteorite. Meteorites are among the oldest objects on Earth — primitive samples of the Solar System's building blocks from 4.6 billion years ago.</p>
